# AST for the Markdown subset used by docs/ (inventory in site/README.md).
# The parser rejects anything outside the subset, doubling as a docs lint.

## Inline markup inside a paragraph, heading, list item, or table cell.
##
## `Del` is `~~struck~~`: the early design notes strike out the non-goals
## that later shipped, and until 2026-10-02 the site printed the tildes.
pub type Inline =
  | Text(s: String)
  | Code(s: String)
  | Bold(items: List[Inline])
  | Em(items: List[Inline])
  | Del(items: List[Inline])
  | Link(label: String, url: String)
derive Show

## One block-level element. List items are themselves block sequences, so
## nested lists and fenced code inside an item come for free.
##
## `Fragment` is a fence marked `skip-check` (a `dawn skip-check` info
## string): code doc-check does not compile because it is not a program on its
## own, such as one half of a two-file project. Its own variant rather than a
## flag on `CodeBlock` because the one place that cares, the renderer, must
## not offer it to the Playground, and a variant makes forgetting that a
## compile error.
##
## `Program` is a whole program that needs some of the repository's packages
## (a `dawn run deps=tileir` info string; `deps` holds the names). doc-check
## runs it as a project and compares its output like any other, so the page
## still shows the two as one window; but the Playground runs one file with
## no packages, so a link would open a program that cannot find its imports.
## A variant for the same reason as `Fragment`: the renderer must not forget.
pub type Block =
  | Heading(level: Int, items: List[Inline])
  | Para(items: List[Inline])
  | CodeBlock(lang: String, body: String)
  | Fragment(lang: String, body: String)
  | Program(lang: String, deps: List[String], body: String)
  | UList(items: List[List[Block]])
  | OList(items: List[List[Block]])
  | Table(header: List[List[Inline]], rows: List[List[List[Inline]]])
  | Quote(blocks: List[Block])
  | Rule
derive Show
